Z||000000||ChadMan||09-14-2001||12:42 AM||||The whole free world, myself included, wants somebody to pay for what's happened in New York.  I am no pacifist, believe me...but I'm sad about what's coming.<P>First of all, we can't just "nuke" Afghanistan.  It's only about the size of Texas, and Pakistan, eastern China and northern India are downwind.  They'd be justifiably outraged if their people started glowing, losing hair and teeth, and having three-eyed babies.  And even if it weren't for fallout, we'd probably just end up killing millions of Afghan goatherders and sheep farmers while bin Laden and the rest of his Taliban bastards took refuge in a bombproof cave in the Afghan mountains.<P>So it looks more and more like we are going to have to mount an air-and-ground assault to seize or kill Osama bin Laden and the leaders of the Taliban government, like terriers driving vermin out of a hole in the ground.  In an effort to stop us, the Taliban will force the dirt-poor, disease-ridden common people of Afghanistan (goat herders and sheep farmers, mostly) to take up arms against us.<P>And we will slaughter them by the thousands, because we have to...just as we were forced into slaughtering the Iraqis and the Vietnamese and the Germans who were simple pawns of megalomaniacs.  Along the way, many brave American troops will lose their lives as well, just as they have since Yorktown and Valley Forge.<P>Naturally we will win the war, because we are powerful, rich, and smart, and most important, because we are morally right.  We only kill when we have to.<P>We will then leave, and the Afghans will return to their mosques and their goat and sheep herds...until the next wacko totalitarian regime takes over and marches them into death again.<P>Think of how many people have died because of totalitarian wackos coming to power.  Stalin...Pol Pot...Hitler...Ho Chi Minh...Idi Amin...Saddam Hussein...the Taliban.  They never learn.<P>War really IS hell, and it is necessary.  <P>Will it ever end?||||reg||9
Z||000001||Urchin||09-14-2001||12:53 AM||||Just to add some of my own thoughts to this...  First of all, from what I have been hearing on the latest news reports...  there have been at least two moments when foot soldiers practically head there foot out the door when called back.  G.W. has called them back on these occasions due to sketchy reports on Bin Laden's where abouts, combined with the fear of potential bloodshed suffered by American soldiers.  Also, just to briefly touch on my personal opinions on this issue, I am one who condemns the idea of war.  However, when your home land is being attacked(and it appears this IS an act of war), then there comes a time when you must defend yourselves, and your country.  I do however have certain opinions as to what provoked these attacks, but unfortunately what's done is done.  You have to deal with "the now".  Which in this case obviously means that it may be necessary to take up arms.  It is unfortunate, I just hope if it comes to that, that casualties (civilian or otherwise) are low. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||09-14-2001||01:14 AM||||No, wars will never end.  There will always be wicked people that rise up and cause them.<P>Didn't people enjoy the past 25 years since vietnam (desert storm--our troops were so awesome, it was practically reduced by their excellence to a skirmish)?<P>Look at just U.S. involvement in the past 100 years.  WWI-1910's.  WWII-1941-1945 for us.  Korean war was TERRIBLE, too.  1950's.  Vietname was terrible-1965-1975.<P>So this last period was a nice break.  People should have seen it as such and appreciated it, instead of thinking it was "the norm".||||reg||1
